Read-only plan critic stage (spec 30): reviews each plan between planning and the loop, approving or sending it back with feedback as `critique` runs.
- `src/server/planCriticService.ts`: critic stage modelled on the evaluator — renders the critic prompt from the card, scoping thread, named spec files and the plan artifacts; runs read-only (planner tool set, no bash); parses `.ralph/CRITIQUE.md` via the shared `parseEvaluation`; approve routes to the loop, revise re-plans with the feedback, capped at 2 consecutive revisions before escalating to plan review; emits `critique.decided`.
- Orchestrator/planning wiring: planning hands off to the critic when `criticEnabled` (per-card `planCritic` override, else `planCriticMode` setting: always/breakdown/off); re-plans inherit critique feedback as the "PREVIOUS ATTEMPT" section; failed critiques retry from needs_attention.
- Settings/schema/UI: `criticProvider`, `criticModel`, `criticReasoningLevel`, `criticTimeoutMinutes`, `criticPromptTemplate`, `planCriticMode`; card columns `plan_critic` and `critic_model`; `critique` run kind surfaced alongside plan/loop/evaluate.
- Mock provider (`src/server/harness/mock.ts`): new `critic` role told apart from the planner by `.ralph/CRITIQUE.md` in the prompt; happy-path approve script and a `critic-revise-once` scenario that revises the first plan and approves the re-plan.
- Tests: `planCriticService.test.ts` unit coverage; `mockPipeline.test.ts` end-to-end critic approve and critic-revise-once runs (critique run rows, transcript `critique.jsonl`, `critique.decided` event, re-plan feedback).
